config MCUX_HAS_COMPONENT_driver.cache_llc
    bool
    default y if MCUX_HW_IP_DriverType_LLC

config MCUX_COMPONENT_driver.cache_llc
    bool "cache_llc"
    select MCUX_COMPONENT_driver.common
    depends on MCUX_HAS_COMPONENT_driver.cache_llc

if MCUX_COMPONENT_driver.cache_llc

    config LLC_MAINTENANCE_TIMEOUT
        int "LLC maintenance operation timeout, in poll iterations (0 = derive)"
        default 0
        help
          How long a cache maintenance operation may take before the driver
          stops waiting and reports kStatus_Timeout, counted in poll-loop
          iterations.

          Leave this at 0 unless you have a reason not to. The driver then
          derives the budget from the cache geometry, which is what bounds the
          work an operation has to do, with margin over the measured worst case
          of every cache entry resident and dirty. Kconfig cannot see the
          device's way and set counts, so it cannot express that derivation
          here.

          A non-zero value replaces the derived budget verbatim. Setting it too
          low makes a maintenance operation that is progressing normally return
          kStatus_Timeout, so only raise it above the derived value - for
          instance if the memory behind the cache is slower than the devices
          this driver was characterized on.

endif
